// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//
// tools/ares-input.bml.in — ares settings template for an automated run.
//
// tools/n64-input.py substitutes @NAME@ with an assignment string of the
// form <sdl-guid>/<slot>/<groupID>/<inputID>[/Lo|/Hi], which is what
// ares' desktop-ui/input/input.cpp parses. The GUID and the indices come
// from probing the virtual pad through libSDL3, not from a table here —
// see that file's header for why.
//
// The `;;` suffix is not decoration: ares stores three bindings per input
// joined by ";" (BindingLimit == 3 in desktop-ui/input/input.hpp), and
// this is the shape it writes itself.
//
// L-Up/L-Down/L-Left/L-Right are absent ON PURPOSE. They address the same
// mapping objects X-Axis/Y-Axis do, and settings.cpp loads the pairs after
// the individual inputs — so listing both here would have the empty one
// silently erase the bound one.

Input
  // A drive run moves windows and takes screenshots, so ares must not be
  // holding input (or the whole emulator) until it is the focused window.
  Defocus: Allow

Nintendo64
  Input
    Controller.Port.@PORT@
      Gamepad
        Up: @DUP@;;
        Down: @DDOWN@;;
        Left: @DLEFT@;;
        Right: @DRIGHT@;;
        B: @B@;;
        A: @A@;;
        C-Up: @CUP@;;
        C-Down: @CDOWN@;;
        C-Left: @CLEFT@;;
        C-Right: @CRIGHT@;;
        L: @L@;;
        R: @R@;;
        Z: @Z@;;
        Start: @START@;;
        X-Axis
          Lo: @XLO@;;
          Hi: @XHI@;;
        Y-Axis
          Lo: @YLO@;;
          Hi: @YHI@;;
